Cell[TextData[{
 "To compile an ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "28feb6dd-a9b9-1548-a85e-ea86fae86bbd"],
 "-ary cyclic tag system to a cyclic tag system, each symbol ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "ca4cb7bc-dd95-0b46-8f43-075a7bfc4fec"],
 " becomes a block of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "143dc93b-5075-d94d-8346-22101b0d7cfa"],
 " cells that are all 0 except for a 1 at position ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["s", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "a6ae6d27-67fd-694d-8bdf-78d3dda10f68"],
 "+1, and each rule part becomes ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "f27abfb8-16c8-9645-a658-86f7c290cefa"],
 " appendants, one for each symbol. Only the 1 in a block makes the cyclic \
tag system append anything, and it does so exactly when the appendant for the \
block's symbol is current. So ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["n", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",ExpressionUUID->
  "a2aac3e2-4079-3443-95d2-29abe5dee4d2"],
 " cyclic tag steps emulate one ",
