 "ModificationHighlight" -> False, "ColorType" -> "", "LinkTrails" -> "", 
  "ExampleCounter" -> 1, 
  "Openers" -> {
   "PrimaryExamplesSection" -> Open, "ExampleSection" -> {"0" -> Open}}, 
  "NewStyles" -> True, "CitationPopupData" -> {"1988", ""}, "ShowCitation" -> 
  False, "RootCaptions" -> "", "HeaderCoreAreaLink" -> {}, 
  "Metadata" -> {
   "built" -> "{2026, 10, 26, 1, 56, 49.3483984}", 
    "history" -> {"1.0", "", "", ""}, "context" -> 
    "EricJamesParfitt`CyclicTagCompiler`", 
    "keywords" -> {
     "cyclic tag system", "n-ary cyclic tag system", "oblivious ring machine",
       "cellular automaton", "automata network", "rule 110", "universality", 
      "compiler", "tutorial"}, "specialkeywords" -> {}, 
    "tutorialcollectionlinks" -> {}, "index" -> True, "label" -> 
    "Eric James Parfitt/ Cyclic Tag Compiler Tech Note", "language" -> "en", 
    "paclet" -> "EricJamesParfitt/CyclicTagCompiler", "status" -> "None", 
    "summary" -> 
    "This tech note explains how CyclicTagCompiler turns cellular automata \
and automata networks into cyclic tag systems, one simple stage at a time, \
and how to decode the evolution of a cyclic tag system back to the evolution \
of the system it emulates. A cyclic tag system is a very simple system that \
can nevertheless do any computation. This has made cyclic tag systems a \
useful step in showing that other simple systems are universal, such as the \
rule 110 cellular automaton and Wolfram's 2,3 Turing machine. There are three \
known routes for compiling Turing machines to cyclic tag systems. One goes \
from a Turing machine to a 2-symbol Turing machine, then to a tag system and \
then to a cyclic tag system. Another goes from a 2-symbol Turing machine to a \
Minsky register machine, then to a Fractran program and then to a cyclic tag \
system. Both are fairly simple, but both encode the state in unary, so the \
cyclic tag system is exponentially slower than the machine it emulates. The \
third route goes through clockwise Turing machines and avoids the exponential \
slowdown, but it is much more complicated.", "synonyms" -> {}, 
    "tabletags" -> {}, "title" -> "Compiling to Cyclic Tag Systems", 
    "titlemodifier" -> "", "metadescription" -> "", "windowtitle" -> 
    "Compiling to Cyclic Tag Systems", "type" -> "Tech Note", "uri" -> 
    "EricJamesParfitt/CyclicTagCompiler/tutorial/CompilingToCyclicTagSystems"}\
},
